This component subscribes to ALL transactions in the app with `useOnyx(ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.TRANSACTION)`, which creates a subscription that will trigger re-renders whenever ANY transaction changes anywhere in the app. This is a significant performance overhead.

**Suggested fix:** Use dedicated hooks from `OnyxListItemProvider` or fetch only the specific transactions needed:

```tsx
// Option 1: If available, use a dedicated hook for selected transactions
const selectedTransactionsData = useSelectedTransactions(selectedTransactionsKeys);

// Option 2: Use individual useOnyx calls for specific transaction keys
// (though this may need to be optimized further depending on the number of transactions)
```

If neither option is available, consider creating a selector that only returns the transactions matching `selectedTransactionsKeys` to minimize unnecessary re-renders.
